6705648,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNjY2NzA1NjQ4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:animation","name":"topic:animation","color":"ffee88","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":1,"created_at":"2026-06-04T15:44:51Z","updated_at":"2026-06-05T08:54:29Z","closed_at":"2026-06-04T19:23:50Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n4.7beta5\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.7.beta5 - Windows 11 (build 26200) - Multi-window, 2 monitors - Direct3D 12 (Forward+) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce RTX 2060 (NVIDIA; 32.0.15.8183) - Intel(R) Core(TM) i7-10750H CPU @ 2.60GHz (12 threads) - 15.84 GiB memory - WASAPI (48000 Hz, Stereo/mono)\n\n### Issue description\n\nWhen I moved to 4.7 and ran my game, I got that issue in-game:\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/ec342b57-7060-48ef-99fb-9ead6d895ab7\n \nI found that this is due to a node I disconnected temporarily in the AnimTree:\n\n<img width=\"1250\" height=\"474\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/e01e58eb-b72b-4519-bd89-c0fcd4f488b6\" />\n\nMoving to 4.7, I had a few breaking changes to fix, but this one really looks like a non desired behaviour. I think that a disconnected node should at best raise a warning, and not an error. When prototyping or testing things out we can be disconnecting and reconnecting things a lot.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nDisconnect a node in the AnimationTree.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nNone.","closed_by":{"login":"TokageItLab","id":61938263,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxOTM4MjYz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61938263?v=4","grav